# Mobile deploy after changes

When modifying any Flutter app in this repo (`dashboard_app`, `entry_app`, `admin_app`):

1. After implementation and before closing the task, **install/run the updated app on the connected Android device**.
2. Use staging Supabase config:
   ```bash
   export SUPABASE_URL=... SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=...
   ./scripts/run_staging_app.sh <dashboard|entry|admin> -d <device_id>
   ```
3. If multiple apps were changed, install the app(s) that were modified.
4. If no device is connected, report that clearly and ask the user to connect the phone.
5. Do not skip mobile install unless the user explicitly says not to deploy.

The user expects updates to be **always installed on their phone** (ثبت التحديث في الجوال).
